{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Cut-and-Bend Kerf Relief Unfolding for HSS &amp; Round Pipe</h2>
          <p>
            Build roll cages, bumpers, and chassis hoops without a mandrel bender. Drop your 3D bent-tube STEP file in to unroll every centerline bend onto straight square HSS or round pipe (<code class="mono">HSS-O</code>). Your torch cuts pie-slice relief slots through three walls, adds corner relief on square tube or rotary unwrap on pipe so thick walls never bind, and leaves the fourth wall intact as a hinge. Pull each bend shut by hand and weld the seams flush with zero grinder fit-up.
          </p>
          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Unfolding Engine</span>
              <span class="value">Auto 3D Spine &amp; Centerline Unwrap</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Relief Cut Control</span>
              <span class="value">Per-Bend Cut Count &amp; Spine Width (<code class="mono">Edge Left</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Supported Stock</span>
              <span class="value">Square/Rect HSS &amp; Round Pipe (HSS-O)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Select <code class="mono">HSS Bending [CUT &amp; BEND]</code> from Quick CAD Fixtures</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Open the <strong>Quick CAD Fixtures</strong> panel on the left sidebar, or drop your own bent-tube <code class="mono">.step</code> file into the upload zone.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Click <span class="ui-chip">HSS Bending [CUT &amp; BEND]</span> at the bottom of <strong>Quick CAD Fixtures</strong>.</li>
              <li>Your 3D bent tube loads with all 3 centerline bends detected and unfolded to a <code class="mono">2030.2 mm</code> straight stick.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 1: Selecting 'HSS Bending [CUT &amp; BEND]' from the left Quick CAD Fixtures panel</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-1-fixture.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-1-fixture.png" alt="Step 1: Selecting HSS Bending [CUT & BEND] in Quick CAD Fixtures" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Select <code class="mono">Bend #1</code> &amp; Click <code class="mono">▸ Cuts (3)</code> Next to Config</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Verify the <span class="ui-chip cyan">Bent Tube Unfolded • 3 BENDS</span> badge on the left sidebar. Use <strong>Profile Override</strong> to switch between <code class="mono">Profile_HSS_Rect</code> and <code class="mono">Round Tube (HSS-O)</code>.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>The bottom table groups each bend (<code class="mono">Bend #1</code>, <code class="mono">Bend #2</code>, <code class="mono">Bend #3</code>) with its angle (<span class="ui-chip">BEND 32.5°</span>), radius (<code class="mono">R=145.0mm</code>), X range (<code class="mono">1384–1466 mm</code>), and spine angle (<code class="mono">180.0° / Spine 0°</code>).</li>
              <li>On <span class="ui-chip">Bend #1</span>, click <span class="ui-chip">▸ Cuts (3)</span> next to <code class="mono">⚙ Bend</code> and <code class="mono">Save</code>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 2: Selecting Bend #1 (32.5°, R=145.0mm) and clicking '▸ Cuts (3)' next to Config</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-2-select-cuts.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-2-select-cuts.png" alt="Step 2: Selecting Bend #1 and clicking Cuts (3) next to Bend Config" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Inspect the Expanded Relief Cuts &amp; Bend Parameters</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Expanding <code class="mono">▸ Cuts (3)</code> shows the three slots in <code class="mono">Bend #1</code>: <code class="mono">Cut 1/3</code> (<code class="mono">1397.5 mm</code>), <code class="mono">Cut 2/3</code> (<code class="mono">1425.0 mm</code>), and <code class="mono">Cut 3/3</code> (<code class="mono">1452.4 mm</code>).
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Tune <strong>Lead-In Strategy</strong> (<code class="mono">Tangent Arc</code>) or <strong>Lead-Out Strategy</strong> (<code class="mono">Circular</code>) per slot if needed.</li>
              <li>On the <code class="mono">Bend #1</code> row, adjust two controls:
                <ul>
                  <li><strong><code class="mono">Cuts</code> (default <code class="mono">3</code>):</strong> Number of wedge relief slots across the bend.</li>
                  <li><strong><code class="mono">Edge Left</code> (default <code class="mono">13.5 mm</code>):</strong> Uncut spine width on the outer wall so the stick holds together and folds cleanly.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 3: Viewing the expanded relief cuts (Cut 1/3..3/3) and inline Cuts / Edge Left controls</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-3-expanded-cuts.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-3-expanded-cuts.png" alt="Step 3: Expanded relief cuts under Bend #1 showing Cuts: 3 and Edge Left: 13.5 mm" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Change <code class="mono">Cuts</code> from <code class="mono">3</code> to <code class="mono">5</code>, Set <code class="mono">Edge Left</code> to <code class="mono">30 mm</code> &amp; Open Cut Preview</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              For a smoother bend curve with smaller wedges and a wider spine, update <code class="mono">Bend #1</code>:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Change <strong><code class="mono">Cuts</code></strong> from <code class="mono">3</code> to <span class="ui-chip">5</span>.</li>
              <li>Change <strong><code class="mono">Edge Left</code></strong> from <code class="mono">13.5</code> to <span class="ui-chip">30.0 mm</span>.</li>
              <li>Click <span class="ui-chip cyan">Save</span> until <span class="ui-chip emerald">Saved ✓</span> appears. Five relief slots (<code class="mono">Cut 1/5</code> through <code class="mono">Cut 5/5</code>) recalculate immediately in the 3D view and G-code.</li>
              <li>Click <span class="ui-chip">⚡ 3D Cut Simulation</span> at the top to inspect the straight stick.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 4: Changing Cuts to 5 and Edge Left to 30.0 mm, saving, and clicking 3D Cut Simulation</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-4-configure-bend.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-4-configure-bend.png" alt="Step 4: Setting Cuts to 5 and Edge Left to 30.0 mm on Bend #1 and clicking 3D Cut Simulation" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 5
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-5">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 05</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Verify the Unfolded Straight Stick in 3D Cut Preview &amp; Click <code class="mono">⬇ Download</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              The <strong>3D Cut Simulation</strong> shows the straight tube (<code class="mono">2030.2 mm</code> long) exactly as it sits in your rotary chuck:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Inspect the 5-Cut Relief Pattern (Center Viewport):</strong> Scrub or play the simulation to confirm all 5 relief slots wrap three walls while leaving the <code class="mono">30.0 mm</code> spine uncut on top.</li>
              <li><strong>Download G-Code (Top-Right Header):</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip emerald">⬇ Download</span> in the <strong>G-Code Post-Processor</strong> bar to save your <code class="mono">.nc</code> file (<code class="mono">3349 lines</code>, <code class="mono">167.5s</code> estimated cut time).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 5: Inspecting the unfolded straight stick in 3D Cut Simulation and clicking '⬇ Download'</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-5-simulate-download.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-5-simulate-download.png" alt="Step 5: 3D Cut Simulation of the unfolded straight stick with 5 relief cuts and clicking Download" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 6
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-6">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 06</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Mandrel / Rotary-Draw Bender Mode (<code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>): Suppress Relief Slots &amp; Scribe Witness Marks</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Running the part on a hydraulic or CNC mandrel / rotary-draw bender instead of cut-and-bend folding? Switch the same bent tube into <strong>Mandrel Bender</strong> mode:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Switch Bend Process Mode:</strong> Under <strong>BEND PROCESS MODE</strong> in the left sidebar, click <span class="ui-chip cyan">Mandrel Bender</span>. RotaryCAM automatically suppresses all relief-cut slots, recalculates the developed straight length (<code class="mono">2020.9 mm</code>) using your die's achieved Centerline Radius (CLR) and elongation factor, and keeps every end cope, miter, and bolt hole intact.</li>
              <li><strong>Pick Your Die &amp; Witness Marks:</strong> Select your matching die (such as <code class="mono">1.5" Sq HSS x 5.5" CLR</code>) and toggle <strong>Start Tangent + Intrados</strong>, <strong>Center / End</strong>, or <strong>Bend Labels (B1, B2)</strong> so the plasma scribe marks exact bend-start tangent lines and pull-direction ticks right on the straight tube before it goes to the bender.</li>
              <li><strong>Reverse Bend Sequence:</strong> Need to feed the tube from the opposite end for clamp-die clearance? Click <span class="ui-chip">Reverse Bend Sequence</span> to mirror all feed lengths and roll angles in one click.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 6: Switching to Mandrel Bender mode to suppress relief slots, scribe witness marks, and preview the LRA Setup Summary</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-6-mandrel-mode.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-6-mandrel-mode.png" alt="Step 6: Mandrel Bender mode active with calibrated die selector, witness mark checkboxes, LRA summary, and scribe G-code" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 7
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-7">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 07</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Calibrate Your Shop Dies in the <code class="mono">Bender Die Library</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Every physical die stretches and springs back slightly differently. Click the <strong>Manage Dies</strong> button next to the Bender Die dropdown to open the <strong>Bender Die Library</strong>:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Built-In &amp; Custom Shop Dies:</strong> RotaryCAM ships with 6 common imperial and metric round/square dies (JD2, RogueFab, Baileigh, and Metric Pipe). Click <span class="ui-chip emerald">+ Add Die</span> or <span class="ui-chip">Edit</span> to dial in your exact shop tooling.</li>
              <li><strong>Calibrated CLR, Elongation &amp; 2-Parameter Springback:</strong> Store nominal vs. achieved CLR, stretch elongation factor, and affine springback (<code class="mono">Yield Offset + deg/90°</code>) plus minimum clamp grip length so every bend angle overbends accurately and tight inter-bend straights trigger clamp-grip warnings before you cut steel.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 7: Calibrating CLR, elongation, 2-parameter springback, and minimum clamp grip in the Bender Die Library</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-7-bender-die-library.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-7-bender-die-library.png" alt="Step 7: Bender Die Library modal listing 6 shop dies with CLR, elongation, yield offset, springback, and min clamp grip" width="2324" height="1397" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 8
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-8">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 08</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Export the 1-Page Printable <code class="mono">LRA / YBC</code> Shop Setup Card (PDF)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Click <span class="ui-chip emerald">Print LRA Setup Card</span> in the <strong>Mandrel Bender LRA Setup Summary</strong> bar to open a clean, 1-page landscape setup sheet formatted for the bender operator:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Mandrel &amp; Tooling Guidance:</strong> Automatically calculates D-factor (<code class="mono">CLR / D</code>) and wall factor (<code class="mono">D / t</code>) to recommend mandrel ball count, nose projection past tangent, wiper die requirement, pressure die assist (PDA) boost, and ERW weld-seam clocking.</li>
              <li><strong>Clamp-Grip &amp; Stub Safety Warnings:</strong> Flags any inter-bend straight or trailing rear collet stub shorter than your die's minimum clamp grip before you load the stick.</li>
              <li><strong>Witness-Mark Schematic &amp; LRA/YBC Table:</strong> Shows every bend zone, Start Tangent X mark, Intrados pull direction (<code class="mono">0°</code> / <code class="mono">180°</code>), incremental carriage feed (<code class="mono">L / Y</code>), roll (<code class="mono">R / B</code>), and springback-compensated bend angle (<code class="mono">A / C</code>) in <code class="mono">mm</code> or <code class="mono">in</code>.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-callout tip" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">Example LRA Setup Card PDF (SM0022 HSS 1-1/2" x 1-1/2")</div>
              <p>
                Inspect a real RotaryCAM setup card exported directly from the <code class="mono">HSS Bending</code> sample fixture:
                <a href="assets/lra-setup-card-sm0022-example.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--cyan-400); font-weight: 600;">Download Example LRA Setup Card (PDF)</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 8: Real exported 1-page landscape LRA / YBC Mandrel Setup Card (SM0022 HSS 1-1/2" x 1-1/2")</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/bending-8-lra-card-example.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/bending-8-lra-card-example.png" alt="Step 8: Real exported RotaryCAM Mandrel / Rotary-Draw LRA Setup Card PDF for SM0022 HSS 1-1/2x1-1/2" width="2324" height="1642" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
